{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-explainer-about-how-to-create-a-viral-idea-meme-or-movement-that-spreads-fast-with-exam/audio/main-6e9b594ee9f0.mp3","durationSec":243.696,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.46,"text":"Virality means that content reaches many people in a short time."},{"start":4.46,"end":8.14,"text":"The content might be an idea, image, video, or written post."},{"start":9.32,"end":14.12,"text":"An internet meme is a cultural item that people copy, change, and share online."},{"start":15.36,"end":20.06,"text":"Use three words to study viral content: **hook, handoff, and change**."},{"start":20.88,"end":22.66,"text":"The hook catches attention quickly."},{"start":23.28,"end":26.48,"text":"The handoff gives someone a simple reason and method to share."},{"start":27.18,"end":29.3,"text":"Change lets people add their own version."},{"start":30.54,"end":35.38,"text":"This last step matters because a meme often grows through participation, not only through watching."},{"start":36.44,"end":41.24,"text":"Your first question should be: “Can someone understand the main idea in a few seconds?”"},{"start":42.24,"end":52.66,"text":"Researcher Jonah Berger described six factors called STEPPS: social currency, triggers, emotion, public, practical value, and stories."},{"start":52.66,"end":63.58,"text":"In simple terms, people may share something because it makes them look interesting, reminds them of something familiar, creates a feeling, is easy to see, is useful, or tells a story."},{"start":63.58,"end":69.04,"text":"Psy released **Gangnam Style** and its music video on 15 July 2012."},{"start":69.88,"end":76.64,"text":"The video went viral in August, and on 21 December it became the first YouTube video to reach one billion views."},{"start":77.6,"end":85.3,"text":"Its strong visual style and memorable performance help us see why public, emotional content can attract attention."},{"start":86.22,"end":91.32,"text":"When planning, choose one or two strong reasons to share instead of using every factor."},{"start":92.02,"end":97.3,"text":"A viral format needs clear rules, but it also needs space for personal change."},{"start":98.02,"end":104.5,"text":"In early February 2013, thousands of **Harlem Shake** videos used a clip from Baauer’s song."},{"start":104.9,"end":112.08,"text":"A typical video showed one dancer and then used a jump cut to show a wild group dance after the bass drop."},{"start":113.24,"end":116.12,"text":"People could recognize the structure and create new versions."},{"start":117.26,"end":120.54,"text":"The **Distracted Boyfriend** meme worked similarly with a picture."},{"start":121.82,"end":124.78,"text":"Antonio Guillem took the stock photograph in 2015."},{"start":126,"end":131.4,"text":"Social media users began using it as a meme in 2017, and it went viral that August."},{"start":132.64,"end":135.82,"text":"Users added different labels to the same visual situation."},{"start":136.52,"end":142.4,"text":"For your format, keep one recognizable pattern and one part that people can easily replace."},{"start":143.5,"end":150.04,"text":"A movement spreads when people can perform a clear action, show that action publicly, and invite the next person."},{"start":151.7,"end":156.2,"text":"In 2014, the **Ice Bucket Challenge** became a viral movement."},{"start":156.7,"end":161.78,"text":"People poured ice water on themselves, posted a video, and asked others to do the challenge or donate."},{"start":162.38,"end":166.12,"text":"It raised money and awareness for ALS and motor neurone disease."},{"start":166.96,"end":171.92,"text":"This example combined a visible action, a serious purpose, and a direct invitation."},{"start":173.36,"end":177.12,"text":"If you create a movement, explain the goal and the next step clearly."},{"start":177.84,"end":181.62,"text":"Make participation safe, honest, and possible for different people."},{"start":182.68,"end":184.86,"text":"Do not pressure people or hide who benefits."},{"start":185.82,"end":189.4,"text":"Fast sharing is valuable only when the message and action are responsible."},{"start":190.64,"end":194.88,"text":"Before a public launch, test your idea with a small group."},{"start":195.8,"end":198.44,"text":"First, show it without a long explanation."},{"start":199.4,"end":200.6,"text":"Can people understand the hook?"},{"start":200.6,"end":204.3,"text":"Next, ask them to share or remake it."},{"start":204.96,"end":206.48,"text":"Can they complete the handoff easily?"},{"start":207.44,"end":209.06,"text":"Finally, compare their versions."},{"start":209.8,"end":212.08,"text":"Is the main idea still clear after the change?"},{"start":212.62,"end":216.82,"text":"Viral marketing also uses social networks so people pass a message to others."},{"start":217.36,"end":224.52,"text":"In 1996 and 1997, Hotmail added a simple tagline to outgoing email and grew very fast."},{"start":225.28,"end":227.48,"text":"Each message carried the invitation forward."},{"start":228.22,"end":234.68,"text":"You can use the same principle without copying the campaign: place a short, natural invitation inside the content."},{"start":235.68,"end":243.16,"text":"Then improve confusing steps and watch meaningful signals such as sharing, remaking, or participation—not only likes."}],"words":[{"text":"Virality","start":0,"end":0.56},{"text":"means","start":0.56,"end":0.86},{"text":"that","start":0.86,"end":1.14},{"text":"content","start":1.14,"end":1.52},{"text":"reaches","start":1.52,"end":1.92},{"text":"many","start":1.92,"end":2.18},{"text":"people","start":2.18,"end":2.54},{"text":"in","start":2.54,"end":2.74},{"text":"a","start":2.74,"end":2.88},{"text":"short","start":2.88,"end":3.02},{"text":"time","start":3.02,"end":3.46},{"text":"The","start":4.46,"end":4.62},{"text":"content","start":4.62,"end":5},{"text":"might","start":5,"end":5.24},{"text":"be","start":5.24,"end":5.44},{"text":"an","start":5.44,"end":5.58},{"text"